    "description": "Replace the CPA Target Type / CPA Target pair with a single numeric Monthly Cap where 0 means unlimited.\n\n=== FIELDS ===\n\n* Monthly Cap — Number. 0 = unlimited.\n\n* DELETE: CPA_Target_Type__c\n\n* DELETE: CPA_Target__c\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Must be a Number, not a picklist. Joyce: 'having this field be a number is going to be super important from a reporting perspective.'\n\n* Cadence is always monthly — 'it's always going to be a monthly cadence.'\n\n* Helper text: 'Enter 0 if there is no cap — the field is numeric so reporting can measure against it.'\n\n* Delete the two old fields. Kobi: 'we can pretty much get rid of a bunch of these fields because the CPA target type we added, so you can choose between amount or unlimited... So we can remove those fields if they're not needed anymore, and they'll just be a monthly cap.'\n\n* Check dependencies before deleting — layouts, list views, reports, flows.\n\n=== NOTES ===\n\n* The original card was title-only. The deletion half is what would have been missed — it's the reason this field exists.\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Aug 11 call — Joyce/Kobi 49:43-50:14\n\nDependencies: None\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nPolished 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
